---Definition of awsCloudFormationStackSet
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetProperties
---@field administrationRoleARN? string The Amazon Resource Number (ARN) of the IAM role to use to create this stack set. Specify an IAM role only if you are using customized administrator roles to control which users or groups can manage specific stack sets within the same administrator account.
---@field autoDeployment? azure.awsconnector.AutoDeployment Describes whether StackSets automatically deploys to AWS Organizations accounts that are added to the target organization or organizational unit (OU). Specify only if PermissionModel is SERVICE_MANAGED.
---@field callAs? azure.awsconnector.CallAs|string Specifies the AWS account that you are acting from. By default, SELF is specified. For self-managed permissions, specify SELF; for service-managed permissions, if you are signed in to the organization's management account, specify SELF. If you are signed in to a delegated administrator account, specify DELEGATED_ADMIN.
---@field capabilities? azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesCapabilitiesList In some cases, you must explicitly acknowledge that your stack set template contains certain capabilities in order for AWS CloudFormation to create the stack set and related stack instances.
---@field description? string A description of the stack set. You can use the description to identify the stack set's purpose or other important information.
---@field executionRoleName? string The name of the IAM execution role to use to create the stack set. If you do not specify an execution role, AWS CloudFormation uses the AWSCloudFormationStackSetExecutionRole role for the stack set operation.
---@field managedExecution? azure.awsconnector.ActiveModel Describes whether StackSets performs non-conflicting operations concurrently and queues conflicting operations.
---@field operationPreferences? azure.awsconnector.OperationPreferences The user-specified preferences for how AWS CloudFormation performs a stack set operation.
---@field parameters? azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesParametersList The input parameters for the stack set template.
---@field permissionModel? azure.awsconnector.PermissionModel|string Describes how the IAM roles required for stack set operations are created. By default, SELF-MANAGED is specified.
---@field stackInstancesGroup? azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesStackInstancesGroupList A group of stack instances with parameters in some specific accounts and regions.
---@field stackSetId? string The ID of the stack set that you're creating.
---@field stackSetName? string The name to associate with the stack set. The name must be unique in the Region where you create your stack set.
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesTagsList The key-value pairs to associate with this stack set and the stacks created from it. AWS CloudFormation also propagates these tags to supported resources that are created in the stacks. A maximum number of 50 tags can be specified.
---@field templateBody? string The structure that contains the template body, with a minimum length of 1 byte and a maximum length of 51,200 bytes.
---@field templateURL? string Location of file containing the template body. The URL must point to a template (max size: 460,800 bytes) that is located in an Amazon S3 bucket.

---In some cases, you must explicitly acknowledge that your stack set template contains certain capabilities in order for AWS CloudFormation to create the stack set and related stack instances.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesCapabilitiesList string[]

---The input parameters for the stack set template.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesParametersList azure.awsconnector.Parameter[]

---A group of stack instances with parameters in some specific accounts and regions.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesStackInstancesGroupList azure.awsconnector.StackInstances[]

---The key-value pairs to associate with this stack set and the stacks created from it. AWS CloudFormation also propagates these tags to supported resources that are created in the stacks. A maximum number of 50 tags can be specified.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsCloudFormationStackSetPropertiesTagsList azure.awsconnector.Tag_5[]

