---Definition of awsEc2Address
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2AddressProperties
---@field allocationId? string <p>The ID representing the allocation of the address.</p>
---@field associationId? string <p>The ID representing the association of the address with an instance.</p>
---@field carrierIp? string <p>The carrier IP address associated. This option is only available for network interfaces which reside in a subnet in a Wavelength Zone (for example an EC2 instance). </p>
---@field customerOwnedIp? string <p>The customer-owned IP address.</p>
---@field customerOwnedIpv4Pool? string <p>The ID of the customer-owned address pool.</p>
---@field domain? azure.awsconnector.DomainTypeEnumValue <p>The network (<code>vpc</code>).</p>
---@field instanceId? string <p>The ID of the instance that the address is associated with (if any).</p>
---@field networkBorderGroup? string <p>The name of the unique set of Availability Zones, Local Zones, or Wavelength Zones from which Amazon Web Services advertises IP addresses.</p>
---@field networkInterfaceId? string <p>The ID of the network interface.</p>
---@field networkInterfaceOwnerId? string <p>The ID of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the network interface.</p>
---@field privateIpAddress? string <p>The private IP address associated with the Elastic IP address.</p>
---@field publicIp? string <p>The Elastic IP address.</p>
---@field publicIpv4Pool? string <p>The ID of an address pool.</p>
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2AddressPropertiesTagsList <p>Any tags assigned to the Elastic IP address.</p>

---<p>Any tags assigned to the Elastic IP address.</p>
