---Definition of awsEc2FlowLog
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2FlowLogProperties
---@field deliverCrossAccountRole? string The ARN of the IAM role that allows Amazon EC2 to publish flow logs across accounts.
---@field deliverLogsPermissionArn? string The ARN for the IAM role that permits Amazon EC2 to publish flow logs to a CloudWatch Logs log group in your account. If you specify LogDestinationType as s3 or kinesis-data-firehose, do not specify DeliverLogsPermissionArn or LogGroupName.
---@field destinationOptions? azure.awsconnector.DestinationOptionsModelProperties Property destinationOptions
---@field id? string The Flow Log ID
---@field logDestination? string Specifies the destination to which the flow log data is to be published. Flow log data can be published to a CloudWatch Logs log group, an Amazon S3 bucket, or a Kinesis Firehose stream. The value specified for this parameter depends on the value specified for LogDestinationType.
---@field logDestinationType? azure.awsconnector.LogDestinationType|string Specifies the type of destination to which the flow log data is to be published. Flow log data can be published to CloudWatch Logs or Amazon S3.
---@field logFormat? string The fields to include in the flow log record, in the order in which they should appear.
---@field logGroupName? string The name of a new or existing CloudWatch Logs log group where Amazon EC2 publishes your flow logs. If you specify LogDestinationType as s3 or kinesis-data-firehose, do not specify DeliverLogsPermissionArn or LogGroupName.
---@field maxAggregationInterval? number The maximum interval of time during which a flow of packets is captured and aggregated into a flow log record. You can specify 60 seconds (1 minute) or 600 seconds (10 minutes).
---@field resourceId? string The ID of the subnet, network interface, or VPC for which you want to create a flow log.
---@field resourceType? azure.awsconnector.ResourceType_2|string The type of resource for which to create the flow log. For example, if you specified a VPC ID for the ResourceId property, specify VPC for this property.
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2FlowLogPropertiesTagsList The tags to apply to the flow logs.
---@field trafficType? azure.awsconnector.TrafficType|string The type of traffic to log. You can log traffic that the resource accepts or rejects, or all traffic.

---The tags to apply to the flow logs.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2FlowLogPropertiesTagsList azure.awsconnector.Tag_11[]

---Definition of awsEc2Image
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImageProperties
---@field architecture? azure.awsconnector.ArchitectureValuesEnumValue <p>The architecture of the image.</p>
---@field blockDeviceMappings? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImagePropertiesBlockDeviceMappingsList <p>Any block device mapping entries.</p>
---@field bootMode? azure.awsconnector.BootModeValuesEnumValue <p>The boot mode of the image. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ami-boot.html'>Boot modes</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field creationDate? string <p>The date and time the image was created.</p>
---@field deprecationTime? string <p>The date and time to deprecate the AMI, in UTC, in the following format: <i>YYYY</i>-<i>MM</i>-<i>DD</i>T<i>HH</i>:<i>MM</i>:<i>SS</i>Z. If you specified a value for seconds, Amazon EC2 rounds the seconds to the nearest minute.</p>
---@field deregistrationProtection? string <p>Indicates whether deregistration protection is enabled for the AMI.</p>
---@field description? string <p>The description of the AMI that was provided during image creation.</p>
---@field enaSupport? boolean <p>Specifies whether enhanced networking with ENA is enabled.</p>
---@field hypervisor? azure.awsconnector.HypervisorTypeEnumValue <p>The hypervisor type of the image. Only <code>xen</code> is supported. <code>ovm</code> is not supported.</p>
---@field imageId? string <p>The ID of the AMI.</p>
---@field imageLocation? string <p>The location of the AMI.</p>
---@field imageOwnerAlias? string <p>The owner alias (<code>amazon</code> | <code>aws-marketplace</code>).</p>
---@field imageType? azure.awsconnector.ImageTypeValuesEnumValue <p>The type of image.</p>
---@field imdsSupport? azure.awsconnector.ImdsSupportValuesEnumValue <p>If <code>v2.0</code>, it indicates that IMDSv2 is specified in the AMI. Instances launched from this AMI will have <code>HttpTokens</code> automatically set to <code>required</code> so that, by default, the instance requires that IMDSv2 is used when requesting instance metadata. In addition, <code>HttpPutResponseHopLimit</code> is set to <code>2</code>. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/configuring-IMDS-new-instances.html#configure-IMDS-new-instances-ami-configuration'>Configure the AMI</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field kernelId? string <p>The kernel associated with the image, if any. Only applicable for machine images.</p>
---@field lastLaunchedTime? string <p>The date and time, in <a href='http://www.iso.org/iso/iso8601'>ISO 8601 date-time format</a>, when the AMI was last used to launch an EC2 instance. When the AMI is used to launch an instance, there is a 24-hour delay before that usage is reported.</p> <note> <p> <code>lastLaunchedTime</code> data is available starting April 2017.</p> </note>
---@field name? string <p>The name of the AMI that was provided during image creation.</p>
---@field ownerId? string <p>The ID of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the image.</p>
---@field platform? azure.awsconnector.PlatformValuesEnumValue <p>This value is set to <code>windows</code> for Windows AMIs; otherwise, it is blank.</p>
---@field platformDetails? string <p>The platform details associated with the billing code of the AMI. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ami-billing-info.html'>Understand AMI billing information</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field productCodes? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImagePropertiesProductCodesList <p>Any product codes associated with the AMI.</p>
---@field public? boolean <p>Indicates whether the image has public launch permissions. The value is <code>true</code> if this image has public launch permissions or <code>false</code> if it has only implicit and explicit launch permissions.</p>
---@field ramdiskId? string <p>The RAM disk associated with the image, if any. Only applicable for machine images.</p>
---@field rootDeviceName? string <p>The device name of the root device volume (for example, <code>/dev/sda1</code>).</p>
---@field rootDeviceType? azure.awsconnector.DeviceTypeEnumValue <p>The type of root device used by the AMI. The AMI can use an Amazon EBS volume or an instance store volume.</p>
---@field sourceInstanceId? string <p>The ID of the instance that the AMI was created from if the AMI was created using <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_CreateImage.html'>CreateImage</a>. This field only appears if the AMI was created using CreateImage.</p>
---@field sriovNetSupport? string <p>Specifies whether enhanced networking with the Intel 82599 Virtual Function interface is enabled.</p>
---@field state? azure.awsconnector.ImageStateEnumValue <p>The current state of the AMI. If the state is <code>available</code>, the image is successfully registered and can be used to launch an instance.</p>
---@field stateReason? azure.awsconnector.StateReason <p>The reason for the state change.</p>
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImagePropertiesTagsList <p>Any tags assigned to the image.</p>
---@field tpmSupport? azure.awsconnector.TpmSupportValuesEnumValue <p>If the image is configured for NitroTPM support, the value is <code>v2.0</code>. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/nitrotpm.html'>NitroTPM</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field usageOperation? string <p>The operation of the Amazon EC2 instance and the billing code that is associated with the AMI. <code>usageOperation</code> corresponds to the <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/Lineitem-columns.html#Lineitem-details-O-Operation'>lineitem/Operation</a> column on your Amazon Web Services Cost and Usage Report and in the <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/price-changes.html'>Amazon Web Services Price List API</a>. You can view these fields on the <b>Instances</b> or <b>AMIs</b> pages in the Amazon EC2 console, or in the responses that are returned by the <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeImages.html'>DescribeImages</a> command in the Amazon EC2 API, or the <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/ec2/describe-images.html'>describe-images</a> command in the CLI.</p>
---@field virtualizationType? azure.awsconnector.VirtualizationTypeEnumValue <p>The type of virtualization of the AMI.</p>

---<p>Any block device mapping entries.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImagePropertiesBlockDeviceMappingsList azure.awsconnector.BlockDeviceMapping[]

---<p>Any product codes associated with the AMI.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImagePropertiesProductCodesList azure.awsconnector.ProductCode[]

---<p>Any tags assigned to the image.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2ImagePropertiesTagsList azure.awsconnector.Tag_12[]

---Definition of awsEc2Instance
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstanceProperties
---@field amiLaunchIndex? number <p>The AMI launch index, which can be used to find this instance in the launch group.</p>
---@field architecture? azure.awsconnector.ArchitectureValuesEnumValue <p>The architecture of the image.</p>
---@field blockDeviceMappings? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesBlockDeviceMappingsList <p>Any block device mapping entries for the instance.</p>
---@field bootMode? azure.awsconnector.BootModeValuesEnumValue <p>The boot mode that was specified by the AMI. If the value is <code>uefi-preferred</code>, the AMI supports both UEFI and Legacy BIOS. The <code>currentInstanceBootMode</code> parameter is the boot mode that is used to boot the instance at launch or start.</p> <note> <p>The operating system contained in the AMI must be configured to support the specified boot mode.</p> </note> <p>For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ami-boot.html'>Boot modes</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field capacityReservationId? string <p>The ID of the Capacity Reservation.</p>
---@field capacityReservationSpecification? azure.awsconnector.CapacityReservationSpecificationResponse <p>Information about the Capacity Reservation targeting option.</p>
---@field clientToken? string <p>The idempotency token you provided when you launched the instance, if applicable.</p>
---@field cpuOptions? azure.awsconnector.CpuOptions <p>The CPU options for the instance.</p>
---@field currentInstanceBootMode? azure.awsconnector.InstanceBootModeValuesEnumValue <p>The boot mode that is used to boot the instance at launch or start. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ami-boot.html'>Boot modes</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field ebsOptimized? boolean <p>Indicates whether the instance is optimized for Amazon EBS I/O. This optimization provides dedicated throughput to Amazon EBS and an optimized configuration stack to provide optimal I/O performance. This optimization isn't available with all instance types. Additional usage charges apply when using an EBS Optimized instance.</p>
---@field elasticGpuAssociations? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesElasticGpuAssociationsList <p>Deprecated.</p> <note> <p>Amazon Elastic Graphics reached end of life on January 8, 2024. For workloads that require graphics acceleration, we recommend that you use Amazon EC2 G4ad, G4dn, or G5 instances.</p> </note>
---@field elasticInferenceAcceleratorAssociations? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesElasticInferenceAcceleratorAssociationsList <p>The elastic inference accelerator associated with the instance.</p>
---@field enaSupport? boolean <p>Specifies whether enhanced networking with ENA is enabled.</p>
---@field enclaveOptions? azure.awsconnector.EnclaveOptions <p>Indicates whether the instance is enabled for Amazon Web Services Nitro Enclaves.</p>
---@field hibernationOptions? azure.awsconnector.HibernationOptions <p>Indicates whether the instance is enabled for hibernation.</p>
---@field hypervisor? azure.awsconnector.HypervisorTypeEnumValue <p>The hypervisor type of the instance. The value <code>xen</code> is used for both Xen and Nitro hypervisors.</p>
---@field iamInstanceProfile? azure.awsconnector.IamInstanceProfile <p>The IAM instance profile associated with the instance, if applicable.</p>
---@field imageId? string <p>The ID of the AMI used to launch the instance.</p>
---@field instanceId? string <p>The ID of the instance.</p>
---@field instanceLifecycle? azure.awsconnector.InstanceLifecycleTypeEnumValue <p>Indicates whether this is a Spot Instance or a Scheduled Instance.</p>
---@field instanceType? azure.awsconnector.InstanceTypeEnumValue <p>The instance type.</p>
---@field ipv6Address? string <p>The IPv6 address assigned to the instance.</p>
---@field kernelId? string <p>The kernel associated with this instance, if applicable.</p>
---@field keyName? string <p>The name of the key pair, if this instance was launched with an associated key pair.</p>
---@field launchTime? string <p>The time the instance was launched.</p>
---@field licenses? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesLicensesList <p>The license configurations for the instance.</p>
---@field maintenanceOptions? azure.awsconnector.InstanceMaintenanceOptions <p>Provides information on the recovery and maintenance options of your instance.</p>
---@field metadataOptions? azure.awsconnector.InstanceMetadataOptionsResponse <p>The metadata options for the instance.</p>
---@field monitoring? azure.awsconnector.Monitoring <p>The monitoring for the instance.</p>
---@field networkInterfaces? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesNetworkInterfacesList <p>The network interfaces for the instance.</p>
---@field outpostArn? string <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Outpost.</p>
---@field placement? azure.awsconnector.Placement <p>The location where the instance launched, if applicable.</p>
---@field platform? azure.awsconnector.PlatformValuesEnumValue <p>The platform. This value is <code>windows</code> for Windows instances; otherwise, it is empty.</p>
---@field platformDetails? string <p>The platform details value for the instance. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/billing-info-fields.html'>AMI billing information fields</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field privateDnsName? string <p>[IPv4 only] The private DNS hostname name assigned to the instance. This DNS hostname can only be used inside the Amazon EC2 network. This name is not available until the instance enters the <code>running</code> state. </p> <p>The Amazon-provided DNS server resolves Amazon-provided private DNS hostnames if you've enabled DNS resolution and DNS hostnames in your VPC. If you are not using the Amazon-provided DNS server in your VPC, your custom domain name servers must resolve the hostname as appropriate.</p>
---@field privateDnsNameOptions? azure.awsconnector.PrivateDnsNameOptionsResponse <p>The options for the instance hostname.</p>
---@field privateIpAddress? string <p>The private IPv4 address assigned to the instance.</p>
---@field productCodes? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesProductCodesList <p>The product codes attached to this instance, if applicable.</p>
---@field publicDnsName? string <p>[IPv4 only] The public DNS name assigned to the instance. This name is not available until the instance enters the <code>running</code> state. This name is only available if you've enabled DNS hostnames for your VPC.</p>
---@field publicIpAddress? string <p>The public IPv4 address, or the Carrier IP address assigned to the instance, if applicable.</p> <p>A Carrier IP address only applies to an instance launched in a subnet associated with a Wavelength Zone.</p>
---@field ramdiskId? string <p>The RAM disk associated with this instance, if applicable.</p>
---@field rootDeviceName? string <p>The device name of the root device volume (for example, <code>/dev/sda1</code>).</p>
---@field rootDeviceType? azure.awsconnector.DeviceTypeEnumValue <p>The root device type used by the AMI. The AMI can use an EBS volume or an instance store volume.</p>
---@field securityGroups? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesSecurityGroupsList <p>The security groups for the instance.</p>
---@field sourceDestCheck? boolean <p>Indicates whether source/destination checking is enabled.</p>
---@field spotInstanceRequestId? string <p>If the request is a Spot Instance request, the ID of the request.</p>
---@field sriovNetSupport? string <p>Specifies whether enhanced networking with the Intel 82599 Virtual Function interface is enabled.</p>
---@field state? azure.awsconnector.InstanceState <p>The current state of the instance.</p>
---@field stateReason? azure.awsconnector.StateReason <p>The reason for the most recent state transition.</p>
---@field stateTransitionReason? string <p>The reason for the most recent state transition. This might be an empty string.</p>
---@field subnetId? string <p>The ID of the subnet in which the instance is running.</p>
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesTagsList <p>Any tags assigned to the instance.</p>
---@field tpmSupport? string <p>If the instance is configured for NitroTPM support, the value is <code>v2.0</code>. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/nitrotpm.html'>NitroTPM</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field usageOperation? string <p>The usage operation value for the instance. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/billing-info-fields.html'>AMI billing information fields</a> in the <i>Amazon EC2 User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field usageOperationUpdateTime? string <p>The time that the usage operation was last updated.</p>
---@field virtualizationType? azure.awsconnector.VirtualizationTypeEnumValue <p>The virtualization type of the instance.</p>
---@field vpcId? string <p>The ID of the VPC in which the instance is running.</p>

---<p>Any block device mapping entries for the instance.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2InstancePropertiesBlockDeviceMappingsList azure.awsconnector.InstanceBlockDeviceMapping[]

