---Definition of awsEc2Ipam
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2IpamProperties
---@field defaultResourceDiscoveryAssociationId? string <p>The IPAM's default resource discovery association ID.</p>
---@field defaultResourceDiscoveryId? string <p>The IPAM's default resource discovery ID.</p>
---@field description? string <p>The description for the IPAM.</p>
---@field ipamArn? string <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IPAM.</p>
---@field ipamId? string <p>The ID of the IPAM.</p>
---@field ipamRegion? string <p>The Amazon Web Services Region of the IPAM.</p>
---@field operatingRegions? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2IpamPropertiesOperatingRegionsList <p>The operating Regions for an IPAM. Operating Regions are Amazon Web Services Regions where the IPAM is allowed to manage IP address CIDRs. IPAM only discovers and monitors resources in the Amazon Web Services Regions you select as operating Regions.</p> <p>For more information about operating Regions, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/ipam/create-ipam.html'>Create an IPAM</a> in the <i>Amazon VPC IPAM User Guide</i>.</p>
---@field ownerId? string <p>The Amazon Web Services account ID of the owner of the IPAM.</p>
---@field privateDefaultScopeId? string <p>The ID of the IPAM's default private scope.</p>
---@field publicDefaultScopeId? string <p>The ID of the IPAM's default public scope.</p>
---@field resourceDiscoveryAssociationCount? number <p>The IPAM's resource discovery association count.</p>
---@field scopeCount? number <p>The number of scopes in the IPAM. The scope quota is 5. For more information on quotas, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/ipam/quotas-ipam.html'>Quotas in IPAM</a> in the <i>Amazon VPC IPAM User Guide</i>. </p>
---@field state? azure.awsconnector.IpamStateEnumValue <p>The state of the IPAM.</p>
---@field stateMessage? string <p>The state message.</p>
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2IpamPropertiesTagsList <p>The key/value combination of a tag assigned to the resource. Use the tag key in the filter name and the tag value as the filter value. For example, to find all resources that have a tag with the key <code>Owner</code> and the value <code>TeamA</code>, specify <code>tag:Owner</code> for the filter name and <code>TeamA</code> for the filter value.</p>
---@field tier? azure.awsconnector.IpamTierEnumValue <p>IPAM is offered in a Free Tier and an Advanced Tier. For more information about the features available in each tier and the costs associated with the tiers, see <a href='http://aws.amazon.com/vpc/pricing/'>Amazon VPC pricing &gt; IPAM tab</a>.</p>

---<p>The operating Regions for an IPAM. Operating Regions are Amazon Web Services Regions where the IPAM is allowed to manage IP address CIDRs. IPAM only discovers and monitors resources in the Amazon Web Services Regions you select as operating Regions.</p> <p>For more information about operating Regions, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/ipam/create-ipam.html'>Create an IPAM</a> in the <i>Amazon VPC IPAM User Guide</i>.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2IpamPropertiesOperatingRegionsList azure.awsconnector.IpamOperatingRegion[]

---<p>The key/value combination of a tag assigned to the resource. Use the tag key in the filter name and the tag value as the filter value. For example, to find all resources that have a tag with the key <code>Owner</code> and the value <code>TeamA</code>, specify <code>tag:Owner</code> for the filter name and <code>TeamA</code> for the filter value.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2IpamPropertiesTagsList azure.awsconnector.Tag_14[]

---Definition of awsEc2KeyPair
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2KeyPairProperties
---@field keyFingerprint? string Property keyFingerprint
---@field keyFormat? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2KeyPairPropertiesKeyFormat|string The format of the key pair. Default: ``pem``
---@field keyName? string A unique name for the key pair. Constraints: Up to 255 ASCII characters
---@field keyPairId? string Property keyPairId
---@field keyType? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2KeyPairPropertiesKeyType|string The type of key pair. Note that ED25519 keys are not supported for Windows instances. If the ``PublicKeyMaterial`` property is specified, the ``KeyType`` property is ignored, and the key type is inferred from the ``PublicKeyMaterial`` value. Default: ``rsa``
---@field publicKeyMaterial? string The public key material. The ``PublicKeyMaterial`` property is used to import a key pair. If this property is not specified, then a new key pair will be created.
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsEc2KeyPairPropertiesTagsList The tags to apply to the key pair.

---The format of the key pair. Default: ``pem``
