---Definition of awsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroup
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupProperties
---@field healthCheckEnabled? boolean Indicates whether health checks are enabled. If the target type is lambda, health checks are disabled by default but can be enabled. If the target type is instance, ip, or alb, health checks are always enabled and cannot be disabled.
---@field healthCheckIntervalSeconds? number The approximate amount of time, in seconds, between health checks of an individual target.
---@field healthCheckPath? string [HTTP/HTTPS health checks] The destination for health checks on the targets. [HTTP1 or HTTP2 protocol version] The ping path. The default is /. [GRPC protocol version] The path of a custom health check method with the format /package.service/method. The default is /AWS.ALB/healthcheck.
---@field healthCheckPort? string The port the load balancer uses when performing health checks on targets.
---@field healthCheckProtocol? string The protocol the load balancer uses when performing health checks on targets.
---@field healthCheckTimeoutSeconds? number The amount of time, in seconds, during which no response from a target means a failed health check.
---@field healthyThresholdCount? number The number of consecutive health checks successes required before considering an unhealthy target healthy.
---@field ipAddressType? string The type of IP address used for this target group. The possible values are ipv4 and ipv6.
---@field loadBalancerArns? azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesLoadBalancerArnsList The Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) of the load balancers that route traffic to this target group.
---@field matcher? azure.awsconnector.Matcher [HTTP/HTTPS health checks] The HTTP or gRPC codes to use when checking for a successful response from a target.
---@field name? string The name of the target group.
---@field port? number The port on which the targets receive traffic. This port is used unless you specify a port override when registering the target. If the target is a Lambda function, this parameter does not apply. If the protocol is GENEVE, the supported port is 6081.
---@field protocol? string The protocol to use for routing traffic to the targets.
---@field protocolVersion? string [HTTP/HTTPS protocol] The protocol version. The possible values are GRPC, HTTP1, and HTTP2.
---@field tags? azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesTagsList The tags.
---@field targetGroupArn? string The ARN of the Target Group
---@field targetGroupAttributes? azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesTargetGroupAttributesList The attributes.
---@field targetGroupFullName? string The full name of the target group.
---@field targetGroupName? string The name of the target group.
---@field targetType? string The type of target that you must specify when registering targets with this target group. You can't specify targets for a target group using more than one target type.
---@field targets? azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesTargetsList The targets.
---@field unhealthyThresholdCount? number The number of consecutive health check failures required before considering a target unhealthy.
---@field vpcId? string The identifier of the virtual private cloud (VPC). If the target is a Lambda function, this parameter does not apply.

---The Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) of the load balancers that route traffic to this target group.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesLoadBalancerArnsList string[]

---The tags.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesTagsList azure.awsconnector.Tag_31[]

---The attributes.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesTargetGroupAttributesList azure.awsconnector.TargetGroupAttribute[]

---The targets.
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsElasticLoadBalancingV2TargetGroupPropertiesTargetsList azure.awsconnector.TargetDescription[]

