---Definition of awsRdsDBSnapshot
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsDBSnapshotProperties
---@field allocatedStorage? number <p>Specifies the allocated storage size in gibibytes (GiB).</p>
---@field availabilityZone? string <p>Specifies the name of the Availability Zone the DB instance was located in at the time of the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field dbInstanceIdentifier? string <p>Specifies the DB instance identifier of the DB instance this DB snapshot was created from.</p>
---@field dbSnapshotArn? string <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field dbSnapshotIdentifier? string <p>Specifies the identifier for the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field dbSystemId? string <p>The Oracle system identifier (SID), which is the name of the Oracle database instance that manages your database files. The Oracle SID is also the name of your CDB.</p>
---@field dbiResourceId? string <p>The identifier for the source DB instance, which can't be changed and which is unique to an Amazon Web Services Region.</p>
---@field dedicatedLogVolume? boolean <p>Indicates whether the DB instance has a dedicated log volume (DLV) enabled.</p>
---@field encrypted? boolean <p>Indicates whether the DB snapshot is encrypted.</p>
---@field engine? string <p>Specifies the name of the database engine.</p>
---@field engineVersion? string <p>Specifies the version of the database engine.</p>
---@field iamDatabaseAuthenticationEnabled? boolean <p>Indicates whether mapping of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) accounts to database accounts is enabled.</p>
---@field instanceCreateTime? string <p>Specifies the time in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) when the DB instance, from which the snapshot was taken, was created.</p>
---@field iops? number <p>Specifies the Provisioned IOPS (I/O operations per second) value of the DB instance at the time of the snapshot.</p>
---@field kmsKeyId? string <p>If <code>Encrypted</code> is true, the Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for the encrypted DB snapshot.</p> <p>The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier is the key ARN, key ID, alias ARN, or alias name for the KMS key.</p>
---@field licenseModel? string <p>License model information for the restored DB instance.</p>
---@field masterUsername? string <p>Provides the master username for the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field multiTenant? boolean <p>Indicates whether the snapshot is of a DB instance using the multi-tenant configuration (TRUE) or the single-tenant configuration (FALSE).</p>
---@field optionGroupName? string <p>Provides the option group name for the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field originalSnapshotCreateTime? string <p>Specifies the time of the CreateDBSnapshot operation in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). Doesn't change when the snapshot is copied.</p>
---@field percentProgress? number <p>The percentage of the estimated data that has been transferred.</p>
---@field port? number <p>Specifies the port that the database engine was listening on at the time of the snapshot.</p>
---@field processorFeatures? azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsDBSnapshotPropertiesProcessorFeaturesList <p>The number of CPU cores and the number of threads per core for the DB instance class of the DB instance when the DB snapshot was created.</p>
---@field snapshotCreateTime? string <p>Specifies when the snapshot was taken in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). Changes for the copy when the snapshot is copied.</p>
---@field snapshotDatabaseTime? string <p>The timestamp of the most recent transaction applied to the database that you're backing up. Thus, if you restore a snapshot, SnapshotDatabaseTime is the most recent transaction in the restored DB instance. In contrast, originalSnapshotCreateTime specifies the system time that the snapshot completed.</p> <p>If you back up a read replica, you can determine the replica lag by comparing SnapshotDatabaseTime with originalSnapshotCreateTime. For example, if originalSnapshotCreateTime is two hours later than SnapshotDatabaseTime, then the replica lag is two hours.</p>
---@field snapshotTarget? string <p>Specifies where manual snapshots are stored: Amazon Web Services Outposts or the Amazon Web Services Region.</p>
---@field snapshotType? string <p>Provides the type of the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field sourceDBSnapshotIdentifier? string <p>The DB snapshot Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that the DB snapshot was copied from. It only has a value in the case of a cross-account or cross-Region copy.</p>
---@field sourceRegion? string <p>The Amazon Web Services Region that the DB snapshot was created in or copied from.</p>
---@field status? string <p>Specifies the status of this DB snapshot.</p>
---@field storageThroughput? number <p>Specifies the storage throughput for the DB snapshot.</p>
---@field storageType? string <p>Specifies the storage type associated with DB snapshot.</p>
---@field tagList? azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsDBSnapshotPropertiesTagListList Property tagList
---@field tdeCredentialArn? string <p>The ARN from the key store with which to associate the instance for TDE encryption.</p>
---@field timezone? string <p>The time zone of the DB snapshot. In most cases, the <code>Timezone</code> element is empty. <code>Timezone</code> content appears only for snapshots taken from Microsoft SQL Server DB instances that were created with a time zone specified.</p>
---@field vpcId? string <p>Provides the VPC ID associated with the DB snapshot.</p>

---<p>The number of CPU cores and the number of threads per core for the DB instance class of the DB instance when the DB snapshot was created.</p>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsDBSnapshotPropertiesProcessorFeaturesList azure.awsconnector.ProcessorFeature_2[]

