---Definition of awsRdsExportTask
---@class azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsExportTaskProperties
---@field exportOnly? azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsExportTaskPropertiesExportOnlyList <p>The data exported from the snapshot or cluster.</p> <p>Valid Values:</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>database</code> - Export all the data from a specified database.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>database.table</code> <i>table-name</i> - Export a table of the snapshot or cluster. This format is valid only for RDS for MySQL, RDS for MariaDB, and Aurora MySQL.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>database.schema</code> <i>schema-name</i> - Export a database schema of the snapshot or cluster. This format is valid only for RDS for PostgreSQL and Aurora PostgreSQL.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>database.schema.table</code> <i>table-name</i> - Export a table of the database schema. This format is valid only for RDS for PostgreSQL and Aurora PostgreSQL.</p> </li> </ul>
---@field exportTaskIdentifier? string <p>A unique identifier for the snapshot or cluster export task. This ID isn't an identifier for the Amazon S3 bucket where the data is exported.</p>
---@field failureCause? string <p>The reason the export failed, if it failed.</p>
---@field iamRoleArn? string <p>The name of the IAM role that is used to write to Amazon S3 when exporting a snapshot or cluster.</p>
---@field kmsKeyId? string <p>The key identifier of the Amazon Web Services KMS key that is used to encrypt the data when it's exported to Amazon S3. The KMS key identifier is its key ARN, key ID, alias ARN, or alias name. The IAM role used for the export must have encryption and decryption permissions to use this KMS key.</p>
---@field percentProgress? number <p>The progress of the snapshot or cluster export task as a percentage.</p>
---@field s3Bucket? string <p>The Amazon S3 bucket where the snapshot or cluster is exported to.</p>
---@field s3Prefix? string <p>The Amazon S3 bucket prefix that is the file name and path of the exported data.</p>
---@field snapshotTime? string <p>The time when the snapshot was created.</p>
---@field sourceArn? string <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the snapshot or cluster exported to Amazon S3.</p>
---@field sourceType? azure.awsconnector.ExportSourceTypeEnumValue <p>The type of source for the export.</p>
---@field status? string <p>The progress status of the export task. The status can be one of the following:</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>CANCELED</code> </p> </li> <li> <p> <code>CANCELING</code> </p> </li> <li> <p> <code>COMPLETE</code> </p> </li> <li> <p> <code>FAILED</code> </p> </li> <li> <p> <code>IN_PROGRESS</code> </p> </li> <li> <p> <code>STARTING</code> </p> </li> </ul>
---@field taskEndTime? string <p>The time when the snapshot or cluster export task ended.</p>
---@field taskStartTime? string <p>The time when the snapshot or cluster export task started.</p>
---@field totalExtractedDataInGB? number <p>The total amount of data exported, in gigabytes.</p>
---@field warningMessage? string <p>A warning about the snapshot or cluster export task.</p>

---<p>The data exported from the snapshot or cluster.</p> <p>Valid Values:</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>database</code> - Export all the data from a specified database.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>database.table</code> <i>table-name</i> - Export a table of the snapshot or cluster. This format is valid only for RDS for MySQL, RDS for MariaDB, and Aurora MySQL.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>database.schema</code> <i>schema-name</i> - Export a database schema of the snapshot or cluster. This format is valid only for RDS for PostgreSQL and Aurora PostgreSQL.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>database.schema.table</code> <i>table-name</i> - Export a table of the database schema. This format is valid only for RDS for PostgreSQL and Aurora PostgreSQL.</p> </li> </ul>
---@alias azure.awsconnector.AwsRdsExportTaskPropertiesExportOnlyList string[]

