---Definition of CloudWatchLogsConfig
---@class azure.awsconnector.CloudWatchLogsConfig
---@field groupName? string <p> The group name of the logs in CloudWatch Logs. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Working-with-log-groups-and-streams.html'>Working with Log Groups and Log Streams</a>. </p>
---@field status? azure.awsconnector.LogsConfigStatusTypeEnumValue <p>The current status of the logs in CloudWatch Logs for a build project. Valid values are:</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>ENABLED</code>: CloudWatch Logs are enabled for this build project.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>DISABLED</code>: CloudWatch Logs are not enabled for this build project.</p> </li> </ul>
---@field streamName? string <p> The prefix of the stream name of the CloudWatch Logs. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Working-with-log-groups-and-streams.html'>Working with Log Groups and Log Streams</a>. </p>

---Definition of ClusterConfig
---@class azure.awsconnector.ClusterConfig
---@field coldStorageOptions? azure.awsconnector.ColdStorageOptions <p>Container for cold storage configuration options.</p>
---@field dedicatedMasterCount? number <p>Number of dedicated master nodes in the cluster. This number must be greater than 2 and not 4, otherwise you receive a validation exception.</p>
---@field dedicatedMasterEnabled? boolean <p>Indicates whether dedicated master nodes are enabled for the cluster.<code>True</code> if the cluster will use a dedicated master node.<code>False</code> if the cluster will not.</p>
---@field dedicatedMasterType? azure.awsconnector.OpenSearchPartitionInstanceTypeEnumValue <p>OpenSearch Service instance type of the dedicated master nodes in the cluster.</p>
---@field instanceCount? number <p>Number of data nodes in the cluster. This number must be greater than 1, otherwise you receive a validation exception.</p>
---@field instanceType? azure.awsconnector.OpenSearchPartitionInstanceTypeEnumValue <p>Instance type of data nodes in the cluster.</p>
---@field multiAZWithStandbyEnabled? boolean <p>A boolean that indicates whether a multi-AZ domain is turned on with a standby AZ. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/managedomains-multiaz.html'>Configuring a multi-AZ domain in Amazon OpenSearch Service</a>. </p>
---@field warmCount? number <p>The number of warm nodes in the cluster.</p>
---@field warmEnabled? boolean <p>Whether to enable warm storage for the cluster.</p>
---@field warmType? azure.awsconnector.OpenSearchWarmPartitionInstanceTypeEnumValue <p>The instance type for the cluster's warm nodes.</p>
---@field zoneAwarenessConfig? azure.awsconnector.ZoneAwarenessConfig <p>Container for zone awareness configuration options. Only required if <code>ZoneAwarenessEnabled</code> is <code>true</code>.</p>
---@field zoneAwarenessEnabled? boolean <p>Indicates whether multiple Availability Zones are enabled. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/managedomains-multiaz.html'>Configuring a multi-AZ domain in Amazon OpenSearch Service</a>.</p>

