---Definition of InstanceMetadataOptionsResponse
---@class azure.awsconnector.InstanceMetadataOptionsResponse
---@field httpEndpoint? azure.awsconnector.InstanceMetadataEndpointStateEnumValue <p>Indicates whether the HTTP metadata endpoint on your instances is enabled or disabled.</p> <p>If the value is <code>disabled</code>, you cannot access your instance metadata.</p>
---@field httpProtocolIpv6? azure.awsconnector.InstanceMetadataProtocolStateEnumValue <p>Indicates whether the IPv6 endpoint for the instance metadata service is enabled or disabled.</p> <p>Default: <code>disabled</code> </p>
---@field httpPutResponseHopLimit? number <p>The maximum number of hops that the metadata token can travel.</p> <p>Possible values: Integers from <code>1</code> to <code>64</code> </p>
---@field httpTokens? azure.awsconnector.HttpTokensStateEnumValue <p>Indicates whether IMDSv2 is required.</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>optional</code> - IMDSv2 is optional, which means that you can use either IMDSv2 or IMDSv1.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>required</code> - IMDSv2 is required, which means that IMDSv1 is disabled, and you must use IMDSv2.</p> </li> </ul>
---@field instanceMetadataTags? azure.awsconnector.InstanceMetadataTagsStateEnumValue <p>Indicates whether access to instance tags from the instance metadata is enabled or disabled. For more information, see <a href='https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/Using_Tags.html#work-with-tags-in-IMDS'>Work with instance tags using the instance metadata</a>.</p>
---@field state? azure.awsconnector.InstanceMetadataOptionsStateEnumValue <p>The state of the metadata option changes.</p> <p> <code>pending</code> - The metadata options are being updated and the instance is not ready to process metadata traffic with the new selection.</p> <p> <code>applied</code> - The metadata options have been successfully applied on the instance.</p>

